## §1 Variable namespace

### Field ownership summary

Every combat variable belongs to exactly one of five owners. The owner
determines its scope, lifetime, and whether reads/writes outside the
designated window are valid. The detailed tables below this row group
fields by *category* (core state, per-slot stats, etc.); this row
groups them by *owner* for the "where does this live?" lookup.

| Owner | Scope it lives on | Lifetime | Variables |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Host** | combat host (PC) character | combat init → combat cleanup | `pod_combat_active`, `pod_combat_is_over`, `pod_combat_round`, `pod_combat_current_actor_team`, `pod_combat_current_actor_position`, `pod_combat_current_ap`, `pod_combat_player_team_size`, `pod_combat_enemy_team_size`, `pod_combat_pc_target_team`, `pod_combat_pc_target_position`, `pod_combat_pc_target_char`, `pod_combat_selected_target_team`, `pod_combat_selected_target_position`, `pod_combat_pc_slot` / `pod_combat_enemy_leader_slot` (the two leader pointer vars — player/0 and enemy/0), `pod_combat_active_slots` (variable list of every filled slot story, appended as slots fill), `pod_combat_winner`, `pod_combat_loser`, `pod_combat_last_damage`, `pod_combat_last_heal_amount`, `pod_combat_last_morale_damage_amount`, `pod_combat_last_morale_heal_amount`, `pod_combat_last_outcome`, `pod_combat_last_attack_result`, `pod_combat_last_retal_fired`, `pod_combat_last_retal_damage`, `pod_combat_last_retal_agg`, `pod_combat_nonfatal_active` |
| **Slot** | `POD_combat_slot` story (one per slot, on Charon) | slot creation → slot cleanup | `combat_team`, `team_position`, `slot_char`, `slot_alive`, `slot_morale`, `slot_prowess`, `slot_soak`, `slot_base_soak`, `slot_hit_chance`, `slot_base_hit_chance`, `slot_initiative`, `slot_init_bonus`, `slot_ap_drain`, `slot_energy_used`, `slot_turn_order`, `slot_has_acted`, `slot_is_guarding`, `slot_is_dodging`, `slot_is_stealthed`, `slot_retaliate_*`, `slot_incorporeal_spirit`, `slot_can_damage_spirit`, all `slot_{stat}_{direction}_{duration}_tier` vars |
| **Workspace (transient)** | combat host | **only between `pod_combat_load_workspace_effect` and `pod_combat_save_workspace_effect`** | `pod_combat_actor_*`, `pod_combat_target_*`, `pod_combat_current_hit_chance` (mirrors of the slot fields above) |
| **Character (AI)** | the acting AI character | persists per-character across combats until `pod_combat_group_cleanup_effect` clears them | `pod_combat_ai_last_move`, `pod_combat_ai_prev_move`, `pod_combat_ai_prev2_move`, `pod_combat_loadout` (variable list) |
| **Log entry** | `POD_combat_log_entry` story (one per log row, on Charon) | combat init → combat cleanup (all entries end together) | `entry.var:outcome`, `entry.var:attack_result`, `entry.var:retal_fired` (three-axis result snapshot — see §4), `entry.var:damage`, `entry.var:heal_amount`, `entry.var:morale_damage_amount`, `entry.var:morale_heal_amount`, `entry.var:retal_damage`, `entry.var:retal_agg`, `entry.var:actor_side` (team code of the acting slot — `0` ally/player / `1` enemy / `-1` system entry; the combat-log GUI keys the ally-gold / enemy-red side bar + actor-name tint off this), `entry.var:self_damage` (post-soak recoil, set only when > 0), `entry.var:aoe_burst_index` (set by AoE iterations so intent segments and the recoil segment render once per move; absent on non-AoE rows), `entry.var:system_message` (only on bookend rows pushed by `pod_combat_push_system_log_effect`), `entry.var:round`, plus the move-context fields the customizable_loc dispatcher reads |

HP is derived live from each slot character's PoD wound vars
(`POD_empty_damage_boxes` etc.); it is **not** owned by any of the
above.

The workspace row is the only one with a sub-action lifetime. The
*Action workspace lifecycle invariant* in §7 spells out the load/save
contract that gives those vars meaning.

### Core state (on the combat host / PC character)

| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `pod_combat_active` | flag: combat is in progress |
| `pod_combat_is_over` | flag: combat is over (re-entry guard) |
| `pod_combat_round` | current round number |
| `pod_combat_current_actor_team` / `_position` | the acting combatant's team (`flag:player` / `flag:enemy`) + position within it (int 0+, 0 = leader) |
| `pod_combat_current_ap` | AP remaining this turn |
| `pod_combat_player_team_size` | count of occupied player positions; incremented as each ally is seated by `POD_combat_duel_add_ally_effect` |
| `pod_combat_enemy_team_size` | count of occupied enemy positions; incremented as each enemy is seated by `POD_combat_duel_add_enemy_effect` |
| `pod_combat_pc_target_team` / `_position` | the PC's persistent target: team + position (never the PC's own player/0) |
| `pod_combat_pc_target_char` | character ref of the PC's current target; read directly by the PC target-name display |
| `pod_combat_selected_target_team` / `_position` | the slot (team + position) loaded into the target workspace |
| `pod_combat_pc_slot` / `pod_combat_enemy_leader_slot` | the two leader pointer vars (player/0 and enemy/0); each resolves to that leader's `POD_combat_slot` story scope. Non-leader slots have no literal pointer var — reach them by matching `combat_team` + `team_position` while iterating `pod_combat_active_slots`. |
| `pod_combat_active_slots` | variable list of slot stories currently in play (filled slots only, in insertion order: player team by position, then enemy team by position). Iterated by every dispatch loop. |

### Per-slot stats (vars on each `POD_combat_slot` story)

| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `combat_team` | flag (`flag:player` / `flag:enemy`): the slot's team, baked at creation |
| `team_position` | int 0+: position within the team (0 = leader, no upper bound), baked at creation |
| `slot_char` | character ref occupying the slot |
| `slot_alive` | 1 while in play, 0 when KO'd. Every in-combat alive→down flip routes through `pod_combat_mark_slot_ko_effect`, which also fires the ally-down morale shock: each still-living teammate loses `pod_combat_ally_down_morale_penalty` (default 2) morale, floored at 1 so the shock alone can never morale-break, and one named system log row posts when at least one teammate was hit |
| `slot_morale` | current Morale |
| `slot_prowess` | current prowess |
| `slot_soak` | live soak chance (0-100) |
| `slot_base_soak` | soak before any tier effects |
| `slot_hit_chance` | live hit chance (20-95). PC slot: refreshed against the PC's currently-selected target every turn start by the `pod_combat_load_workspace_effect` writeback. NPC slots: rotates between leader-baseline, last-attack-target, and last-attacker-retaliation depending on the most recent workspace flush — only stable for the PC. The combat-window slot card hides this absolute value for NPCs and shows the signed net tier modifier (`pod_combat_slot_hit_net_mod_value`) instead, dispatched through `PODCombatSlotHitDisplay`. |
| `slot_base_hit_chance` | hit chance before any tier effects |
| `slot_initiative` | initiative roll this round |
| `slot_init_bonus` | next-round initiative modifier |
| `slot_ap_drain` | pending AP drain: consumed (floor 0) at the victim's next turn start, then cleared. Writes are take-max. A drain >= base AP (`ap_drain_6`) is the stun — 0 AP means no affordable move, so the turn is lost. Drives the dazed status icon + dazed/stunned log rows |
| `slot_energy_used` | counter for AI energy-attrition weighting |
| `slot_turn_order` | turn-rank within the round (1 = first); stamped by `pod_combat_calc_turn_orders_effect` after initiative roll |
| `pod_combat_turn_order_list` (host var list) | the round's alive slots in turn order, rebuilt by `pod_combat_build_turn_order_list_effect` right after the ranks are stamped - the initiative track datamodels it directly (GUI cannot sort, so display order = list order) |
| `slot_has_acted` | 1 once the slot's turn resolves this round; reset to 0 by `pod_combat_calculate_initiative_effect` at the start of every round |
| `slot_dot_amount` / `slot_dot_rounds` | active burn (DoT): damage per round-end tick / rounds remaining. Absence = no burn (the tick loop filters on `has_variable = slot_dot_rounds`); re-application overwrites |
| `slot_dot_kind` | LITERAL flag typing the burn: `flag:morale`, a damage source (`flag:fire` etc.), or `flag:duel` for untyped. Always set while a burn is active — status icon, log dispatch, and wound dispatch all read it |
| `slot_dot_aggravated` | 0/1, always set with the burn: when 1, untyped ticks route as `duel_aggravated` (mirrors the move's `damage_type = aggravated`); ignored for typed sources (PoD's classifier types those per victim splat) |
| `slot_controlled` | mind control pending: the slot's next AI turn serves the other side (target selection inverts once, then the marker clears). Set by §13c, consumed by `pod_combat_execute_ai_turn_effect`. Players are never marked (immune at application) |

Team affiliation is stored explicitly on each slot as the `combat_team`
flag (`flag:player` / `flag:enemy`); `team_position` (int 0+, 0 = leader)
gives the position within that team. There is no flat slot index.

**Health is NOT stored on the slot story.** Live script values
derive HP from each slot character's PoD wound vars. The slot
story only holds the `slot_char` pointer; the SVs read
`POD_empty_damage_boxes` / `POD_total_damage_boxes` /
`POD_health_aggravated_damage_num` off the character:

| SV | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `pod_combat_slot_hp_value` | empty wound boxes (HP remaining) |
| `pod_combat_slot_max_hp_value` | wound track length (max HP) |
| `pod_combat_slot_agg_damage_sv` | aggravated wound boxes |
| `pod_combat_slot_total_damage_sv` | total wound boxes filled |

> **Why not cached?** Caching HP on the slot story was tried earlier
> and rejected. Stale cache between turns vs PoD's wound writes
> caused constant desync. Deriving HP live keeps display and
> gameplay reads in lockstep with PoD's canonical state.
>
> The one sanctioned exception is the **wound-bar display mirror**
> (`slot_mirror_total` / `_agg` / `_maxhp`): the combat window reads
> these plain slot vars instead of the `*_sv` chain for perf, and they
> are refreshed from the SVs at every HP-change chokepoint. Display-only,
> never a logic source. See *HP cache rejected* in §7.

