All persist across rounds; only cleared when consumed or at combat end.

| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `slot_is_guarding` | Guard stance active |
| `slot_is_dodging` | Dodge stance active |
| `slot_is_stealthed` | Stealth active (includes the `pod_combat_stealth_hit_bonus` hit bonus, default +30) |
| `slot_retaliate_hit` | retaliation damage if hit |
| `slot_retaliate_miss` | retaliation damage if missed |
| `slot_retaliate_{hit,miss}_agg` | aggravated variants |

### Per-slot spirit-damage capability

| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `slot_incorporeal_spirit` | slot character is incorporeal; physical attacks no-op unless the attacker has `slot_can_damage_spirit` |
| `slot_can_damage_spirit` | slot character can land physical hits on incorporeal targets |

### Tier variables (on the `POD_combat_slot` story)

Tier = 1 (small, ±10), 2 (medium, ±20), 3 (large, ±30). Live stats
are rebuilt from base + sum of active tier magnitudes. See the
**Tier system** section below.

```
slot_{stat}_{direction}_{duration}_tier
  stat:      soak | hit
  direction: buff | debuff
  duration:  round (cleared at round end) | combat (lasts the fight)
```

### Action workspace (transient — acting combatant + current target)

Mirrors the per-slot fields for whoever is currently acting / targeted.
Lives on the combat host so saved scopes / scripted-effect parameters
can read it without crossing into the slot-story scope.

| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `pod_combat_actor_*` | actor's stats (loaded from `current_actor` slot) |
| `pod_combat_target_*` | target's stats (loaded from `selected_target` slot) |
| `pod_combat_current_hit_chance` | active attacker's hit chance this attack |

Most tier, stance, retaliation, and `base_*` fields exist on both sides -
load/save effects walk slot stories and write into / read back from the
matching workspace mirror. Those mirrors are symmetric: every such field
(including `slot_init_bonus`, `slot_ap_drain`, and `slot_energy_used`) is
loaded and saved on BOTH the actor and target side. Both sides flow
through one parametric pair, `pod_combat_load_side_from_story_helper` /
`pod_combat_save_side_to_story_helper` (`SIDE = actor|target`); the four
public load/save effects (`load_actor` / `load_target` / `save_actor` /
`save_target`) are thin wrappers over them.

Exception - the two spirit-capability flags are LOAD-ONLY.
`slot_can_damage_spirit` / `slot_incorporeal_spirit` are mirrored at load
but deliberately NOT written back at save: they are write-once facts set in
`pod_combat_init_slot_from_character_effect` (from `POD_can_damage_spirit_trigger`
/ `POD_can_be_killed_physically_trigger`, static trait/perk/artifact facts) and
never mutate mid-fight, so the slot copy can't diverge from the mirror. A move
that changed spirit capability mid-fight would break this and need both a
save-helper writeback and a slot-story writer.

A few fields only have a live reader on one side (e.g. `slot_energy_used`
feeds the actor-side AI energy-attrition weighting; the target-side
mirror is no-op overhead), but they're mirrored anyway for shape
uniformity — one helper body, no per-field branching.

When you add a new slot field, mirror it on both sides (one line in each
helper). See §11 *Adding a new workspace mirror field*.

**Lifecycle contract:** These variables are valid ONLY between a
`pod_combat_load_workspace_effect` call and the matching
`pod_combat_save_workspace_effect`. Any other code path that reads
them is reading stale data — canonical per-combatant state lives on
the slot story. See §7 *Action workspace lifecycle invariant* for
the full statement and enforcement strategy.

