## §5 Tier system

Static buff/debuff infrastructure for `soak` and `hit_chance`. Lives
in `pod_combat_tier_effects.txt`.

### Data model

Tier state lives in two layers — the slot story and the
workspace mirror (read/written by skill effects).

**Slot story (persistent for the combat):**

| Var | Role |
|---|---|
| `slot_base_soak` | soak before any tier effects |
| `slot_base_hit_chance` | hit chance before any tier effects |
| `slot_soak` | live soak (base + buff mags − debuff mags) |
| `slot_hit_chance` | live hit chance (same formula) |
| `slot_{stat}_{direction}_{duration}_tier` | current tier (1/2/3) for that stat × direction × duration tuple |

**Workspace (loaded from the active slot each action):**

| Var | Role |
|---|---|
| `pod_combat_actor_base_soak` / `pod_combat_target_base_soak` | mirror of the slot's `slot_base_soak` |
| `pod_combat_actor_soak` / `pod_combat_target_soak` | mirror of `slot_soak` |
| `pod_combat_actor_base_hit_chance` / `pod_combat_target_base_hit_chance` | mirror of `slot_base_hit_chance` |
| `pod_combat_actor_hit_chance` / `pod_combat_target_hit_chance` | mirror of `slot_hit_chance` |
| `pod_combat_actor_{stat}_{direction}_{duration}_tier` / `pod_combat_target_{stat}_…_tier` | mirror of the matching slot tier var |

Stat is `soak` or `hit`, direction is `buff` or `debuff`, duration is
`round` (cleared at round end) or `combat` (cleared at combat end).

### Magnitudes

| Tier | Magnitude |
|---:|---|
| 1 (small) | ±10 |
| 2 (medium) | ±20 |
| 3 (large) | ±30 |

### Apply / revert flow (recalc-from-base, no deltas)

- **Applying tier N:** set the tier var, then call a recalc effect.
  The stat is rebuilt from base + sum of active tier magnitudes,
  clamped on write. Clamping losses do NOT accumulate because each
  apply and each revert starts from the pristine base.
- **Round end:** round-duration tier vars are cleared, then every
  slot is recalculated. Combat-duration tiers persist.
- **Combat end:** all tier vars cleared.

### When to edit `pod_combat_tier_effects.txt` directly

- The tier stat categories change (currently `soak`, `hit`).
- Tier magnitudes change (the ±10/20/30 small/medium/large values).
  These are single-sourced: the `combat_tier_small_mag` /
  `combat_tier_medium_mag` / `combat_tier_large_mag` script_values in
  `pod_combat_values.txt` are cross-file constants read by name (NOT
  `@`-macros) everywhere they apply: `pod_combat_tier_effects.txt`
  (workspace/slot recalc), the GUI display SVs in `pod_combat_values.txt`,
  and `POD_soak_chance` in `POD_health_track_values.txt` (the soak the wound
  pipeline actually rolls). Retune by editing those three SV definitions only;
  there is no lockstep to maintain. The move-side tier setters in
  `pod_combat_move_init_effects.txt` carry only the tier ORDINAL (1/2/3), not 
  the magnitude. Stealth's hit bonus is also outside it: a single designer-tunable SV,
  `pod_combat_stealth_hit_bonus` (default 30, `pod_combat_values.txt`),
  feeds the recalc core's STEALTH_BONUS param and the slot-recalc mirror.

