## §8 Internal milestone glossary

Internal labels still surface in commit history and code comments
where ripping them out would lose context. Decode here.

| Tag | Refactor | What changed |
|---|---|---|
| **A9** | Result-flag collapse | Replaced the 11 separate `pod_combat_last_was_*` presence flags with a single result variable. Closed by B1 (initially as an int, later migrated to a flag value — see "Result-flag model migration" below). |
| **A10** | Damage-helper scope redirect | Damage helpers used to write to fixed `pod_combat_last_*` host vars. The scope-redirect proposal would parameterize each helper to write to a caller-provided var, removing the snapshot/restore pattern in §8 self-damage. Mostly closed by B1; full closure is one parameter per helper × every caller × every damage source — not worth the surface for one consumer. |
| **B1** | Result consolidation (Wave 4) | Single-variable result model. Cut the §8 self-damage snapshot from three fields to two; cleanup is one `remove_variable` instead of eleven; PODCombatLogResultText dispatch reads one branch per outcome instead of priority-walking flag presence. Originally implemented with an integer code (0..12 + reserved rcode 4); subsequently migrated to flag values for self-documentation. |
| **B2** | Unified contact resolver (Wave 4) | Pre-B2 each damage source had its own dispatcher (fire / sun / silver / gold / holy / etc.). Replaced by capability-flag-driven contact resolver: every move walks the same spirit-gate → stealth → dodge → hit-roll → guard chain, branching only at damage application by `damage_source`. |
| **B3** | Capability flags emitted by generator (Wave 4) | Per-move capability flag set (`checks_spirit_gate`, `requires_hit_roll`, `checks_guard`, `checks_stance`) emitted at generator time as `attack_type` defaults + per-move `override_*` columns. Made the runtime read flags directly without dispatching off `var:attack_type`. |
| **B4** | Rider condition gate (Wave 4) | Added `heal_condition` / `morale_damage_condition` / `self_damage_condition` columns. Phases §7-§9 read partition triggers against `pod_combat_last_result` to make their payload conditional on the §6 outcome. Pre-B4 the heal step gated drain inline on `_hp_damage_trigger`; B4 made the condition author-controlled. |
| **B5** | Reaction phase (Wave 4) | Added §15 reaction phase. Initially gated retaliate-on-contact on `_hp_damage_trigger` (codes 0/6/7); switched to `_contact_trigger` (codes 0/1/2/6/7) post-B5 because thorns-style stances should fire on guard-blocked / soaked too. Retaliate-on-miss extended from code 3 only to codes 3/5/12 (miss / dodge / stealth — same semantic). |
| **B6** | AoE team-side filters (Wave 4) | Added the AoE iteration target-alive check + team-side filter so `team_enemy` / `team_ally` moves walk only the right side and skip KO'd slots. |
| **Wave 4** | Umbrella name for B1-B6 | The 2026 Q1 push that consolidated rcodes, unified the contact resolver, introduced capability flags, the rider condition gate, the reaction phase, and the AoE filters. |

